# D18. Every direct module this tree may depend on, one path per line. The gate
# diffs the module graph against this file, so taking a new dependency is a
# visible change here rather than a line in go.mod nobody reads.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# The parent proposal's table says why each one is not the standard library.
# The one it commits to that has not arrived: x/sync.
#
# An entry here is a module the tree actually imports. Listing one it does not
# makes the gate fail closed on a dependency nobody took, which is how the
# TOML parser sat here for phases after every setting moved into the database.

golang.org/x/sys

# Argon2id password hashing, XChaCha20-Poly1305 at rest and MD4 for the SMB NT
# hash, none of which the standard library provides. Arrived with Phase 3's
# auth subsystem.
golang.org/x/crypto

# NFC and NFD candidate spellings, so a name another program wrote in either
# form is found as it is written. Arrived with Phase 1's path layer. The
# encoding subpackages joined it for the legacy code pages a zip entry and an
# older client can arrive in, which is a set of conversion tables rather than
# anything a program should carry its own copy of.
golang.org/x/text

# ICU's character-set detector, ported. It answers the one question x/text
# cannot: which of CP949, Shift_JIS, GBK and Big5 a name is written in, when
# the format that carried it declares nothing. A zip entry without the UTF-8
# flag is exactly that case, and statistical detection over the whole set of
# names in one archive is what turns it into a decodable answer.
github.com/gogs/chardet

# SQLite, translated to Go rather than wrapped, which is what keeps
# CGO_ENABLED=0 and with it the static binary and the toolchain-free cross
# build. Arrived with Phase 2's store.
modernc.org/sqlite

# The directory ETag hash, which is wire-visible so parity keeps it BLAKE3.
# Pure Go, so CGO_ENABLED=0 has no fallback to disable. Arrived with Phase 4's
# aggregate; Phase 6 reuses it for the client-selected upload checksum, which
# is why it is one entry here and one direct dependency rather than two.
lukechampine.com/blake3

# BMP, TIFF and WebP decoding for the preview worker. The standard library
# covers JPEG, PNG and GIF; these three are what x/image adds, and all of them
# are pure Go, which is what keeps the decoders out of a C library and
# CGO_ENABLED=0 with nothing to fall back to. Arrived with Phase 9.
golang.org/x/image

# zstd for the search index's block compression. Pure Go, so CGO_ENABLED=0 has
# nothing to fall back to, and the format is what the two implementations agree
# on rather than the encoder's exact output. It enters the graph with Phase 8;
# the parent proposal's table lists it against Phase 9, which is the phase that
# was expected to need it first.
github.com/klauspost/compress

# The change channel for /api/v1/events. The dependency decision was reopened
# because the protocol carries client frames (sub/unsub), so a hand-rolled
# frame layer would re-implement control-frame handling, close codes and
# fragmentation that a maintained module already owns.
#
# It serves the old tree only. gorilla upgrades over net/http, and the engine
# runs on fasthttp, which exposes no Hijacker for gorilla to take the socket
# through. This entry leaves with internal/.
github.com/gorilla/websocket

# The same change channel on the engine's transport. It is the gorilla API
# over fasthttp rather than a second protocol implementation, which is what
# makes the wire frames and the authorization behaviour carry across unchanged.
#
# Confined to engine/http and the assembly by the layer gate, which matches
# the whole gofiber organization rather than the framework's own path: this
# module serves requests, and that is what the rule is about.
github.com/gofiber/contrib/websocket

# The presentation layer's HTTP engine, replacing the hand-rolled net/http
# stack. Settled as D2 before phase 3 began, and importable only under
# engine/http, which the layer gate enforces.
#
# Its transport (fasthttp, bytebufferpool, tcplisten) arrives with it but is
# not listed: this file names direct modules, and nothing here imports those
# three by name.
github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2
